{
  "findings": [
    {
      "file": "vertical-pod-autoscaler/pkg/recommender/routines/recommender.go",
      "line": 159,
      "severity": "P2",
      "message": "Record GC completion only after successful cleanup. Advancing lastCheckpointGC before calling GC suppresses retries after listing or deletion failures until the GC interval elapses. Restore an error result from GarbageCollectCheckpoints and update the timestamp only on success.",
      "evidence": "Lines 158–160 unconditionally advance the timestamp before GC. cluster_feeder.go:294–310 returns early on either listing failure, and :323–325 logs deletion failures without reporting them to the caller. The previous code preserved lastCheckpointGC on error. With the default config.go:116 interval, failed cleanup now postpones another attempt for ten minutes."
    },
    {
      "file": "vertical-pod-autoscaler/pkg/recommender/routines/recommender.go",
      "line": 190,
      "severity": "P2",
      "message": "Start separate timeouts for checkpoint writing and GC. The single deadline now covers both sequential operations, so writing can consume GC's entire budget. Create GC's timeout after StoreCheckpoints returns, using the parent context and the independently configured GC duration.",
      "evidence": "RunOnce creates one deadline at lines 190–192. MaintainCheckpoints passes that same context first to StoreCheckpoints at :156 and then to GC at :160. checkpoint_writer.go:115–118 checks cancellation only after processing a VPA, and :134 waits for workers, so writing can return after the deadline. GC then receives an expired context and passes it to Delete at cluster_feeder.go:323. The diff removes the previously independent GC timeout and its configuration."
    }
  ],
  "coverage": "Reviewed TASK.json, CHANGE.diff, all changed production hunks, the supplied checkpoint writer, and the controller caller/configuration wiring. Confirmed two distinct contract violations. Moving the write deadline to immediately before MaintainCheckpoints preserves its normal RunOnce start point and was not reported separately.",
  "limitations": [
    "Read-only source review only; no tests were run.",
    "External client, lister, and checkpoint API helper implementations are unavailable. Actual request cancellation and broader operational consequences were not verified.",
    "No additional supplied production caller demonstrates consequences of removing timeout creation from direct MaintainCheckpoints calls."
  ],
  "contribution": "Established failed-GC retry suppression from the timestamp gate and feeder failure branches. Confirmed shared-budget exhaustion using the writer's cancellation checks and worker wait, while avoiding a claim that the write timeout forcibly interrupts in-flight API calls.",
  "next_action": "finalize"
}
